                <head>No. 59.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jarvis to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-12"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 12, 1888</date>.
                        (Received June 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 128.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 126, of April 18, 1888,
                    I now have the honor to inclose the translation made by Mr. Williams, the
                    secretary of the legation, of the law concerning trademarks.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos J.
                        Jarvis</hi>.</signed></closer>






